Z||000000||CoryFiero||11-04-2001||11:54 PM||||OK first of all I have a 1984 Fiero but it has a 1987 engine in it, its still a 4 cyl.<BR>When I took it to get the oil changed (I dont know how :|) Well I told them it was an 84 (duh im stupid) when I should have said 87 I dont know what i was thinking, well will this make any difference in the oil change or not?<P>Thanx<P>cory<P>Also is an 84SE a "aero" fiero?||65.28.255.134||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||11-05-2001||12:20 AM||||Hmmm...good question. I dont own any 4 bangers (yet, Im getting an Indy on Weds though), so Im not real sure.  I used to have an 89 Buick Skylark w/ the tech 4 engine which is what they used on 87/88 Fieros also. It had an internal oil filter, where as the 84s had an external. So your engine may differ in that aspect. Im assuming by your post that you already had it done, so I guess they figured that much out.<BR>Im kinda afraid that you may be in for some headaches in the future...you own a 17 year old car (w/ a 14 year old engine) and you dont even know how to change the oil...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> Id suggest doing alot of reading of this forum! Itll help. Good luck, and welcome to the forum.<BR>BTW, 84 Fieros arent aero, except for the Indys.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My7logo_1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 11-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||11-05-2001||01:06 AM||||It's my understanding that some of the very early 84's had a smaller oil capacity   listed, along with a differently marked dipstick. In other words, it called for 3 qts of oil. It was changed later and a different stick used. If there is a sticker on the underside of your decklid, a service tech might see 3 qts listed and not add enough enough oil. I think this is the way I read it anyway.<BR>Don ||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierospeeder||11-05-2001||01:43 AM||||there was a recall done on the 84s.<P><BR>The 84s got a larger capacity oil filter, and they take 5 quarts of oil.  <P><BR>I got an 84 at home. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||watts||11-05-2001||01:53 AM||||The oil filter moving inside the pan didn't happen until '88 on these.<P>And any place that changes oil and doesn't check the stick for level after (i.e. relying soley on capacity stickers) should be sued out of business.  That'd be just plane and simple ignorance on there part.<P>Oh, one thing you should know though (and they might not!) is that you should be using the V6 oil filter, not the usual 4cyl one.  The 6's is larger and gives more filter area, and a hair more capacity of oil.<BR><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid||||reg||1
